# INV-13 — invented. Four overs a side: deliveries that are not one of the over.
# Edge cases (Law 17.3.2.5: a fielder returning without leave, fielding the
# ball illegally, or distracting the striker): the delivery is bowled and
# faced but is no ball of the over, no ball in the bowler's figures, and the
# over goes on past it; the five penalty runs go to the batting side and are
# nobody's to bowl; the runs that stand do rotate the strike (3, odd), and
# a bye or a leg bye that stands is a bye or a leg bye; a bowler's over of
# six dots with one such delivery in it is still a maiden (over 1: seven
# deliveries, 1-1-0-0); a free hit passed over by one (a no-ball, the not-
# in-the-over bye, then the bowled that the free hit saves); a free hit
# that follows a no-ball and a distraction, and is hit for six.
match INV-13
title Four overs, deliveries not in the over
date 2026-11-13
overs 4
